research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.prompt.md-3293-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.prompt.md-3294-**Given:** A natural $m \ge 1$, reals $a \le b$, an integrable $f : [a,b] \to \mathbb{R}^{m}$ with components $f_0,\dots,f_{m-1}$, and the vector $v := \int_a^b f \in \mathbb{R}^{m}$; write $g(t) := \sum_{i<m} f_i(t)^{2}$, so that $\lVert f(t)\rVert_2 = \sqrt{g(t)}$ ([[def-euclidean-inner-product]], [[def-p-norms-on-rn]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.prompt.md-3295-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.prompt.md:3296:[L1] The vector-valued integral is componentwise: $f$ is integrable exactly when every $f_i$ is bounded and Darboux integrable, and then $\bigl(\int_a^b f\bigr)_i = \int_a^b f_i$; $\int_a^a f = 0$ ([[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]], [[def-darboux-integral]], [[def-oriented-integral]], [[def-bounded-set]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.prompt.md-3297-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.prompt.md-3298-[L2] Linearity of the integral: integrable functions on $[a,b]$ are closed under sums and scalar multiples, and $\int_a^b(\lambda u + \mu w) = \lambda\int_a^b u + \mu\int_a^b w$ ([[thm-linearity-of-the-integral]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.prompt.md-3299-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.prompt.md-3300-[L3] Monotonicity of the integral: for $a<b$ and integrable $u \le w$ on $[a,b]$, $\int_a^b u \le \int_a^b w$; and an integrable $u \ge 0$ has $\int_a^b u \ge 0$ ([[thm-monotonicity-of-the-integral]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.prompt.md-3301-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound.prompt.md-3302-[L4] Products and squares: if $u,w$ are integrable on $[a,b]$ then so are $|u|$, $u^{2}$ and $uw$ ([[cor-integrability-of-absolute-values-products-and-lattice-operations]]).
