--
items/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-113-
items/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-114-- **The lower bound is deliberately crude.** The inequality $\sqrt{1+u} \ge 1 + u/\iota(3)$ used in step 1.4 holds for $0 \le u \le \iota(3)$ and is far from sharp; it is chosen because it is polynomial, so that step 2.3 is an application of [[cor-primitives-of-a-continuous-function]] and nothing more. The exact value of $\int_0^1\sqrt{1+t^{2}+t^{4}}\,dt$ is not a value this page can name.
items/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-115-
items/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md:116:- **The sequence and the integral are independent computations**, put in one item because they exercise the two halves of [[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]] on the same space. Neither uses the other.
--
