research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl-7-{"id":"cex-the-mean-value-inequality-is-attained","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"L1 claims every constant function has derivative zero, but the cited lemma only gives this for x to the zero power, the constant 1. Thus step 1.1's derivative claim for f1 equal to 0 is not licensed by its cited fact.","context_sha256":"9c7bb68ed62e155dfaf57e66afbbcf0ceaac0959377688831fc15facb064b1c5","item_sha256":"5793b0383afd870320f8aae4a9cab7efdd50f51a0f3fb62792711456e8eb9304","at":"2026-08-10T02:40:24.817Z"}
research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl-8-{"id":"cor-uniform-cauchy-criterion-function-series","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"[L3] asserts the finite-sum identity relating a tail to two partial sums, but def-series-of-real-functions only defines the partial sums and does not state that subtraction identity. No finite-sum splitting law is cited to support it.","context_sha256":"a116c6803468c8ac5c2b779ed1049b2e6ea4436363ca573c7362c2acaa8897c7","item_sha256":"42c3dbfb1359815833f86cc03da6c716bf3a85e5c05b8432cd24989084541560","at":"2026-08-10T02:40:26.246Z"}
research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl:9:{"id":"def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"The restriction claim says f is integrable on every closed subinterval, including a degenerate [c,c]. But this definition defines integrability only for a<b, and the cited subinterval lemma requires c<d; its remarks explicitly leave the degenerate case to the oriented integral convention.","context_sha256":"6a2ab77f8208dca0e1a3c3d26b1d474b3b2bb2863c49edc7c8daa380649263af","item_sha256":"c3c3b00ab208524e52321af57ca99dd448ba8fb826ac84fd3be3e72e598ce017","at":"2026-08-10T02:40:30.250Z"}
